* A medial ''*-r-'' in {{cog|och|-}} should correspond to a pre-initial in {{cog|tbq|-}}, but this is not present ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).
* A final ''*-k'' is present in {{cog|tbq|-}} yet absent in {{cog|och|-}}, which is an irregular correspondence ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}; {{zh-ref|Sagart, 2011b}}).

Alternatively, {{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} considers {{w|Waic languages|Waic}} {{m|und|*bras||wild boar}} a better match. Meanwhile {{zh-ref|Sagart (2011b)}} suggests {{cog|bo|བ||female cattle}} and {{cog|qvy|bra||female cattle}} as possible comparanda; if so, a semantic analogy would be {{och-l|豬|pig}}, possibly a rural dialectal variant (from the sound changes *''ʈa'' < *''tra'' < *''Cra'') of {{och-l|豭|male pig}} and its homophone {{och-l|麚|stag}}, with *''kra'' meaning "male animal" generally ({{zh-ref|Wang, 1982}}; {{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

